# LinguaHub AI - Docker build context exclusions (Phase 11).
# Keeps secrets, dev tooling, and unrelated distribution artifacts out of
# the build context entirely - not just out of the final image (excluding
# them here means they're never even sent to the Docker daemon / never
# available to any build stage to accidentally COPY).

# Secrets - never enter the build context under any circumstance.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.key
serviceAccountKey.json
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
*.serviceaccount.json
android/app/google-services.json

# Version control and editor state.
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea

# Node dependencies - reinstalled fresh in the build stage (npm ci), never
# copied from the host (avoids leaking host-specific native bindings and
# dev-only devDependencies into the build context).
node_modules

# Test/dev-only artifacts - never needed by the running backend image.
tests
e2e
docs
*.md

# Desktop/mobile distribution paths - unrelated to this backend image.
android
capacitor.config.json
main.js
dist
build

# Local build/output noise.
*.log
npm-debug.log*
